Lab 5: Parameterizing a Pipeline
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Understand the concept of pipeline parameterization in OpenShift • Modify existing Tekton pipelines to accept dynamic parameters • Configure parameters for image tags, repository URLs, and deployment configurations • Execute parameterized pipelines with custom values • Validate that pipeline parameters are correctly applied during execution • Implement best practices for pipeline parameter management

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of OpenShift and Kubernetes concepts • Familiarity with Tekton Pipelines and Tasks • Knowledge of YAML syntax and structure • Experience with command-line interface (CLI) tools • Completion of previous labs covering basic pipeline creation • Understanding of container images and tags

