Task 1: Understanding Pipeline Parameters
Subtask 1.1: Review Current Pipeline Structure
First, let's examine your existing pipeline to understand its current structure.

Connect to your OpenShift cluster:
oc login --server=https://your-cluster-url --token=your-token
Switch to your project namespace:
oc project your-project-name
List existing pipelines:
tkn pipeline list
View your current pipeline definition:
tkn pipeline describe build-and-deploy-pipeline
Subtask 1.2: Identify Parameterization Opportunities
Examine your pipeline and identify hardcoded values that should be parameterized:

Export current pipeline to YAML:
oc get pipeline build-and-deploy-pipeline -o yaml > current-pipeline.yaml
Review the pipeline file:
cat current-pipeline.yaml
Look for hardcoded values such as: • Image names and tags • Repository URLs • Deployment names • Resource limits

Task 2: Modify Pipeline to Accept Parameters
Subtask 2.1: Create Parameterized Pipeline Definition
Create a new pipeline definition with parameters.

Create a new pipeline file:
cat > parameterized-pipeline.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: tekton.dev/v1beta1
kind: Pipeline
metadata:
  name: parameterized-build-deploy
  namespace: your-project-name
spec:
  params:
    - name: git-url
      type: string
      description: Git repository URL
      default: "https://github.com/your-username/sample-app.git"
    - name: git-revision
      type: string
      description: Git revision to checkout
      default: "main"
    - name: image-name
      type: string
      description: Name of the container image
      default: "sample-app"
    - name: image-tag
      type: string
      description: Tag for the container image
      default: "latest"
    - name: deployment-name
      type: string
      description: Name of the deployment
      default: "sample-app-deployment"
    - name: registry-url
      type: string
      description: Container registry URL
      default: "image-registry.openshift-image-stream.svc:5000"
  workspaces:
    - name: shared-data
    - name: git-credentials
      optional: true
  tasks:
    - name: fetch-source
      taskRef:
        name: git-clone
        kind: ClusterTask
      workspaces:
        - name: output
          workspace: shared-data
        - name: basic-auth
          workspace: git-credentials
      params:
        - name: url
          value: $(params.git-url)
        - name: revision
          value: $(params.git-revision)
    - name: build-image
      taskRef:
        name: buildah
        kind: ClusterTask
      runAfter:
        - fetch-source
      workspaces:
        - name: source
          workspace: shared-data
      params:
        - name: IMAGE
          value: "$(params.registry-url)/$(context.pipelineRun.namespace)/$(params.image-name):$(params.image-tag)"
        - name: DOCKERFILE
          value: "./Dockerfile"
    - name: deploy-application
      taskRef:
        name: openshift-client
        kind: ClusterTask
      runAfter:
        - build-image
      params:
        - name: SCRIPT
          value: |
            oc set image deployment/$(params.deployment-name) \
              $(params.deployment-name)=$(params.registry-url)/$(context.pipelineRun.namespace)/$(params.image-name):$(params.image-tag)
            oc rollout status deployment/$(params.deployment-name)
EOF
Subtask 2.2: Apply the Parameterized Pipeline
Apply the new pipeline:
oc apply -f parameterized-pipeline.yaml
Verify the pipeline was created:
tkn pipeline describe parameterized-build-deploy
Check the parameters section:
tkn pipeline describe parameterized-build-deploy | grep -A 20 "Params"
Subtask 2.3: Create Workspace Resources
Create the necessary workspace resources for the pipeline.

Create a PersistentVolumeClaim for shared data:
cat > pipeline-workspace-pvc.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: pipeline-workspace-pvc
spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 1Gi
EOF
Apply the PVC:
oc apply -f pipeline-workspace-pvc.yaml
Task 3: Pass Parameters When Running the Pipeline
Subtask 3.1: Run Pipeline with Default Parameters
First, test the pipeline using default parameter values.

Create a PipelineRun with default parameters:
cat > pipelinerun-default.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: tekton.dev/v1beta1
kind: PipelineRun
metadata:
  name: parameterized-run-default
spec:
  pipelineRef:
    name: parameterized-build-deploy
  workspaces:
    - name: shared-data
      persistentVolumeClaim:
        claimName: pipeline-workspace-pvc
EOF
Execute the pipeline run:
oc apply -f pipelinerun-default.yaml
Monitor the pipeline execution:
tkn pipelinerun logs parameterized-run-default -f
Subtask 3.2: Run Pipeline with Custom Parameters
Now run the pipeline with custom parameter values.

Create a PipelineRun with custom parameters:
cat > pipelinerun-custom.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: tekton.dev/v1beta1
kind: PipelineRun
metadata:
  name: parameterized-run-custom
spec:
  pipelineRef:
    name: parameterized-build-deploy
  params:
    - name: git-url
      value: "https://github.com/your-username/custom-app.git"
    - name: git-revision
      value: "develop"
    - name: image-name
      value: "custom-application"
    - name: image-tag
      value: "v1.2.3"
    - name: deployment-name
      value: "custom-app-deployment"
  workspaces:
    - name: shared-data
      persistentVolumeClaim:
        claimName: pipeline-workspace-pvc
EOF
Execute the custom pipeline run:
oc apply -f pipelinerun-custom.yaml
Monitor the execution:
tkn pipelinerun logs parameterized-run-custom -f
Subtask 3.3: Use CLI to Start Pipeline with Parameters
You can also start pipelines directly using the Tekton CLI.

Start pipeline with CLI parameters:
tkn pipeline start parameterized-build-deploy \
  --param git-url="https://github.com/your-username/another-app.git" \
  --param git-revision="feature-branch" \
  --param image-name="feature-app" \
  --param image-tag="feature-v1.0.0" \
  --param deployment-name="feature-deployment" \
  --workspace name=shared-data,claimName=pipeline-workspace-pvc \
  --showlog
List all pipeline runs:
tkn pipelinerun list
Task 4: Verify Parameter Usage
Subtask 4.1: Examine Pipeline Run Details
Verify that the pipeline correctly uses the passed parameters.

Get detailed information about a pipeline run:
tkn pipelinerun describe parameterized-run-custom
Check the parameters section in the output:
tkn pipelinerun describe parameterized-run-custom | grep -A 10 "Params"
View the task runs and their parameters:
oc get taskruns -l tekton.dev/pipelineRun=parameterized-run-custom -o yaml | grep -A 5 -B 5 "params:"
